{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBQdDLzdUUcU73rRr6i7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 16 (Al 0.21 / Sb 0.79)** as the best composition. Its EQE was 0.011%, the highest of the three I measured. All three results are near zero, so the photoresponse across this library is weak at 2.1 eV.\n\n| Index | Composition (Al/Sb) | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 10 | 0.51 / 0.49 | −0.0012 |\n| **16** | **0.21 / 0.79** | **0.011** |\n| 20 | 0.11 / 0.89 | 0.0006 |\n\n- **How I chose what to measure:** I spent all 5 XRD scans first, on indices 4, 7, 10, 13 and 16. Every scan had the same two strong peaks, which are probably from the substrate. Index 10 also showed weak peaks that match a rutile-type AlSbO4 phase, and index 13 had a weaker version of one of them. That made index 10 my first merit measurement, but its EQE was essentially zero.\n- **Remaining two measurements:** Index 16 on the Sb-rich side did better. I then measured index 20 at the far Sb-rich end to see if it kept improving, but EQE dropped again. The best composition probably lies somewhere between indices 10 and 20.\n- **Not measured:** The 18 other compositions have no merit values, including indices 11–15 and 17–19 close to the result. I didn't spend merit measurements on the Al-rich end (indices 0–7), since I expected aluminium oxide there to be insulating and not absorb 2.1 eV light. That's an assumption, not a measurement, so the true best in the library could be one of the unmeasured compositions.\n\nBoth budgets are used up and the submission was accepted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":548,"cache_read_input_tokens":7409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":548},"output_tokens":576,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnos